        "content": "<p>I am working on a project that verifies a model for an extension of λ-calculus.  The syntax for the extension has a necessary use of mutual induction.  Here is a simple example of this induction:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">module</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">expose</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">section</span>\n\n<span class=\"c\">/-</span><span class=\"cm\">!</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">Smallest true mutual induction Lean accepts and the toolchain `con-ron --verified` declines.</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">`I.sw` takes a function returning `B`, and `B.b` takes an `I`, so neither can be defined first.</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">-/</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">mutual</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"kn\">inductive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"kn\">inductive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">end</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>This <strong>checks</strong> in Lean 4 (<code>lake build</code> and <a href=\"https://live.lean-lang.org/#codez=LYewJgrgNgpgUHAAgbRgDwA4gM4wLoAEGEARlAJYDGBulALuSAHYID0AtAIRwDKwAhlFjY6BOgCcIMAsAh0IgguSaR6jJgQAyMfhv6VKMDHWwFdYMQAtpdECCiVL%2FZQQAGlZu3HMC7dgDcYcXIAM3IYMFcCMBhKCiYYbAA6OFcASSTsAHcoun4Aa0SzAhCIJjUfcRh5cSZlAHM3ACFXABozFWakklyCot03NLaaEAIE8jprcQJKAZJpGLCEizDxERT2VgRZeUE4AiUVCDVAgjSCAC4CAAVvDAIsqfgDg4AfGizLggAKADl%2BUSAJMICE0AJQEYFpfaHVQMU5NL63ED3R5BZ4vd4kL7nYFNOAwFRAA\">Lean 4 playground</a>).  It is <strong>rejected</strong> by <code>con-ron</code> with exit 2 and message</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">con</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">ron</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">declined</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">process</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">model</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">of</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">reflexive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">member</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"c1\">--verified)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p><strong>Question for Palomar maintainers</strong>: This will fail in Palomar.  Is mutual induction out of scope for Palomar?</p>",
        "id": 629271470,
        "sender_full_name": "Lars Ericson",
        "timestamp": 1791212136
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><strong>Note 1:</strong> There is a workaround.  I don't think it is as clear as the <code>mutual</code> syntax but it will pass <code>con-ron</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">inductive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Arm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">inductive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Arm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">i</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">b</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p><strong>Note 2:</strong> If anything in <code>mathlib</code> uses <code>native-decide</code> or <code>mutual</code>, those uses may fail <code>con-ron</code> and hence Palomar.</p>",
